# `awaitCaptureReceiver(t).await(captureContext = awaitCaptureFlag())` — a captureContext argument that SUSPENDS
# (GitHub #64). The await marker is excluded from the stage-0 operand plan (SuspendOperandPlan.cs) because it
# reconstructs its own operands, so the ordering rule that plan enforces everywhere else is EmitAwaitPoint's own
# obligation here — and this document is its only emitted-shape witness. Kotlin evaluates the awaitable receiver
# before the argument; the argument's suspension then splits the marker in half, so the receiver's value must be in
# a state-machine field before the suspension rather than left in the ConfigureAwait slot, where it would be
# evaluated after the resume instead (`awaitCaptureReceiver` would run on the wrong side of it).
#
# The receiver CALL, evaluated into the bound field ahead of the suspension:
